    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33132" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ossĕus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		2. os, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of bone</i>, <i>bone-</i> (post Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cuneus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col. 5,
					11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cultelli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					12, 25, 54, § 115</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Like bone</i>, <i>hard as bone</i>,
				<i>bony</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv. 5,
					53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ilex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					16, 38, 73, § 186</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cutis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 10, 30</span></i>
			.</div>
